Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: ipu6: IPU4P: update the iwake watermark after the
 stream is off

The watermark update reaches IPU4P firmware through the proxy queue. Sent
before the stream flush while a large frame is being written (Surface Pro
7 front camera at full resolution), it stalls that frame: the flush and
close are never acknowledged and both time out (2 s each, every stop).
Updating it after set_streaming(0) gives clean stops (0 timeouts in 12).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-queue.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-queue.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-queue.c
index 38db162d6..c1611ed45 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-queue.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-queue.c
@@ -582,7 +582,14 @@ static void stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 
 	mutex_lock(&stream->mutex);
 
-	ipu6_isys_update_stream_watermark(av, false);
+	/*
+	 * IPU4P: the watermark update goes to the firmware through the proxy
+	 * queue. Sent while a large frame is still being written (the Surface
+	 * Pro 7 front camera at full resolution) it stalls that frame, so the
+	 * stream flush is never acknowledged. Update it once the stream is off.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_IPU4P(av->isys->adev->isp))
+		ipu6_isys_update_stream_watermark(av, false);
 
 	mutex_lock(&av->isys->stream_mutex);
 	if (stream->nr_streaming == stream->nr_queues && stream->streaming)
@@ -590,6 +597,9 @@ static void stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 	list_del(&aq->node);
 	mutex_unlock(&av->isys->stream_mutex);
 
+	if (IS_IPU4P(av->isys->adev->isp))
+		ipu6_isys_update_stream_watermark(av, false);
+
 	stream->nr_streaming--;
 	stream->streaming = 0;
 	mutex_unlock(&stream->mutex);
-- 
